# CRM SaaS

## Mục tiêu

CRM (Customer Relationship Management) là hệ thống quản lý tương tác với khách hàng và quản lý sales pipeline. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, CRM SaaS là một trong những core business applications được xây dựng, tập trung vào việc quản lý leads, contacts, accounts, opportunities, và customer interactions. Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc implement một CRM system hiệu quả với các features cần thiết cho sales teams.

Một CRM system hiệu quả cần kết hợp giữa data management, workflow automation, reporting, và user experience. Rule này cover từ data modeling, business logic, đến frontend design và integration patterns.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Data Model Design**

Model leads, contacts, accounts properly. Define relationships clearly. Use appropriate data types. Plan for scalability. Include audit fields.

**2. Lead Management**

Track lead lifecycle. Define lead sources. Implement lead scoring. Enable lead assignment. Track lead activities.

**3. Opportunity Pipeline**

Design pipeline stages. Track opportunity progress. Calculate win probabilities. Forecast revenue. Measure conversion rates.

**4. Activity Tracking**

Log all interactions. Track emails, calls, meetings. Link to records. Include notes. Enable search.

**5. Workflow Automation**

Automate repetitive tasks. Define triggers and actions. Create approval workflows. Enable notifications. Monitor automation.

**6. Reporting và Analytics**

Track KPIs. Measure performance. Enable custom reports. Create dashboards. Forecast revenue.

**7. Integration Capabilities**

Integrate with email. Connect telephony. Link to ERP. Sync calendar. Enable API access.

**8. User Experience**

Intuitive interface. Quick data entry. Easy navigation. Mobile responsive. Accessible design.

**9. Data Security**

Role-based access. Field-level security. Record ownership. Audit logging. Data encryption.

**10. Scalability**

Design for data growth. Use efficient queries. Implement archiving. Enable multi-tenancy. Plan for scale.

## Checklist

- [ ] Data model designed
- [ ] Lead management implemented
- [ ] Opportunity pipeline configured
- [ ] Activity tracking set up
- [ ] Workflow automation created
- [ ] Reporting system built
- [ ] Integration APIs configured
- [ ] UI/UX designed
- [ ] Security measures implemented
- [ ] Performance tested

## Anti Pattern

**1. Overly Complex Data Model**

Too many custom fields. Complex relationships. Performance issues. Hard to maintain. Simplify design.

**2. Ignoring User Adoption**

Complex workflows. Poor UX. Low adoption. Train users. Simplify processes.

**3. No Data Validation**

Invalid data. Inconsistent records. Poor quality. Validate all inputs.

**4. Siloed Information**

No sharing. Duplicate efforts. Poor collaboration. Enable team sharing.

**5. Manual Data Entry**

Time-consuming. Errors. Poor efficiency. Automate data capture. Integrate systems.

